IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pic-dates`
IMPORT `pic-commission`

-- Personal Injury Commission Act 2020 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in pic-commission.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each
-- assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Dates are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the date`

`WC` MEANS `the Workers Compensation Division`
`MA` MEANS `the Motor Accidents Division`
`POSS` MEANS `the Police Officer Support Scheme Division`

`lawyer` MEANS `an Australian legal practitioner`
`union officer` MEANS `an officer of an organisation of employers or employees registered under the Industrial Relations Act 1996`
`federal association officer` MEANS `an officer of an association of employers or employees registered under the Fair Work Act 2009`
`insurer employee` MEANS `a person employed by a licensed insurer or former licensed insurer or by a self-insurer`
`law practice employee` MEANS `a person employed by a law practice`
`friend` MEANS `someone else`

`efficiency` MEANS `the representation would let the matter be dealt with more efficiently given its complexity`
`unable` MEANS `it would be unfair because the insurer cannot represent itself effectively`
`fairness` MEANS `it would be unfair given fairness between the insurer and the other parties`
`no ground` MEANS `no ground the Commission is satisfied of`

`direction` MEANS `a direction to produce documents or provide information or give a consent`
`summons` MEANS `a summons to attend a conference or hearing`
`WC evidence` MEANS `a requirement to give evidence on oath or answer a question in the Workers Compensation Division`
`POSS evidence` MEANS `a requirement to give evidence on oath or answer a question in the Police Officer Support Scheme Division`

`in time` MEANS `I complied with the direction in time`
`late with excuse` MEANS `I did not comply in time but had a reasonable excuse, so section 49 makes it no offence and does not keep the material out`
`late without excuse` MEANS `I did not comply in time without reasonable excuse, so it is an offence and I cannot have the material admitted`
`not yet due` MEANS `the time for complying has not yet run out`

`WID court` MEANS `court proceedings on a claim for work injury damages`
`WID excepted` MEANS `court proceedings under section 235A or 235C of the 1998 Act or for fraud under the Crimes Act 1900 on such a claim`
`motor court` MEANS `court proceedings on a motor accident claim`
`motor excepted` MEANS `court proceedings under Division 6.6 of the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017 or Part 4.6 of the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999`
`other court` MEANS `other court proceedings`

`MAC damages` MEANS `a claim for damages under the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999`
`MAI benefits` MEANS `a claim for statutory benefits under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017`
`MAI damages` MEANS `a claim for damages under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017`
`police claim` MEANS `a claim under the police officer support scheme`
`workers claim` MEANS `a claim for workers compensation or work injury damages under the 1998 Act`
`other claim` MEANS `some other claim`

`IRO in time` MEANS `the Officer dealt with my complaint in time`
`IRO late` MEANS `the Officer did not deal with my complaint in time`
`IRO pending` MEANS `the time for dealing with my complaint has not yet run out`

§§ `s 31(5) -- outside the State`

#ASSERT `Can my proceedings be conducted outside New South Wales` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my proceedings be conducted outside New South Wales` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my proceedings be conducted outside New South Wales` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my proceedings be conducted outside New South Wales` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 48 -- representation`

-- Arguments: Division, representative, refused for lack of authority.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be represented by this person` `WC` `lawyer` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 48(2) is about agents; a lawyer is entitled whatever the agent rule.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be represented by this person` `MA` `lawyer` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be represented by this person` `WC` `union officer` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be represented by this person` `WC` `federal association officer` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be represented by this person` `WC` `insurer employee` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be represented by this person` `WC` `law practice employee` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be represented by this person` `WC` `union officer` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 48(8) "means": a friend is not an agent in the Workers Compensation Division.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be represented by this person` `WC` `friend` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "agent" undefined in the other Divisions.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be represented by this person` `MA` `union officer` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be represented by this person` `POSS` `friend` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be represented by this person` `MA` `friend` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Arguments: 1998 Act claim, I have a lawyer, leave granted, ground, leave revoked.
#ASSERT `May the insurer be represented by a lawyer` TRUE FALSE FALSE `no ground` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the insurer be represented by a lawyer` TRUE TRUE FALSE `no ground` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the insurer be represented by a lawyer` FALSE FALSE FALSE `no ground` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the insurer be represented by a lawyer` TRUE FALSE TRUE `efficiency` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the insurer be represented by a lawyer` TRUE FALSE TRUE `unable` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the insurer be represented by a lawyer` TRUE FALSE TRUE `fairness` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 48(4) "only if satisfied": leave on no ground does not count.
#ASSERT `May the insurer be represented by a lawyer` TRUE FALSE TRUE `no ground` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 48(5) revoked.
#ASSERT `May the insurer be represented by a lawyer` TRUE FALSE TRUE `efficiency` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Am I entitled to an interpreter or other assistance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to an interpreter or other assistance` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Must the Commission take my lawyer's written submission into account` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Commission take my lawyer's written submission into account` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must the Commission take my lawyer's written submission into account` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 49 -- the direction, as a regulative rule`

-- Arguments: day given, last day allowed, complied, day complied, today, reasonable excuse. Direction given 1 March 2026,
-- to comply by 15 March 2026.
#ASSERT `Did I comply with the direction in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 15 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 20 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Did I comply with the direction in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 15 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 20 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `in time`
-- The day after the last day.
#ASSERT `Did I comply with the direction in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 15 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 16 3 2026) (`d` 20 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `late without excuse`
#ASSERT `Did I comply with the direction in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 15 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 16 3 2026) (`d` 20 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS `late with excuse`
-- Not complied: the last day itself, and the day after.
#ASSERT `Did I comply with the direction in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 15 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 15 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `not yet due`
#ASSERT `Did I comply with the direction in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 15 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 16 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `late without excuse`
#ASSERT `Did I comply with the direction in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 15 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 16 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS `late with excuse`
-- Across a year end: given 20 December 2026, due 5 January 2027, complied 5 January.
#ASSERT `Did I comply with the direction in time` (`d` 20 12 2026) (`d` 5 1 2027) TRUE (`d` 5 1 2027) (`d` 6 1 2027) FALSE EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Did I comply with the direction in time` (`d` 20 12 2026) (`d` 5 1 2027) TRUE (`d` 6 1 2027) (`d` 6 1 2027) FALSE EQUALS `late without excuse`

#ASSERT `Can I have the document or information admitted` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I have the document or information admitted` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I have the document or information admitted` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 49(3), 51, Sch 3 cl 8, Sch 3A cl 6 -- offences`

-- Arguments: requirement, Division, I am a party, the answer would incriminate me, reasonable excuse.
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` `direction` `WC` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` `direction` `WC` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` `direction` `MA` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` `summons` `WC` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` `summons` `MA` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 51(2): in the Motor Accidents Division a summons may be issued only to a party.
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` `summons` `MA` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` `WC evidence` `WC` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` `WC evidence` `WC` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` `POSS evidence` `POSS` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` `POSS evidence` `POSS` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Self-incrimination is about answers, not summonses.
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` `summons` `WC` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `The most I can be fined in penalty units` `direction` EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `The most I can be fined in penalty units` `summons` EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `The most I can be fined in penalty units` `WC evidence` EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `The most I can be fined in penalty units` `POSS evidence` EQUALS 50

