-- Arguments: day made, longer period notified, day notified, last day of the longer period.
-- 31 January 2026 + 30 days = 2 March 2026 (February 2026 has 28 days).
#ASSERT `By what day must my complaint be dealt with` (`d` 31 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `d` 2 3 2026
-- Notice on the 30th day, of a period ending 30 March: extended.
#ASSERT `By what day must my complaint be dealt with` (`d` 31 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 2 3 2026) (`d` 30 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 30 3 2026
-- Notice on the 31st day: too late to extend.
#ASSERT `By what day must my complaint be dealt with` (`d` 31 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 3 3 2026) (`d` 30 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 2 3 2026
-- A "longer" period that ends sooner is ignored.
#ASSERT `By what day must my complaint be dealt with` (`d` 31 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 2 2026) (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 2 3 2026
-- Across a year end: 15 December 2026 + 30 days = 14 January 2027.
#ASSERT `By what day must my complaint be dealt with` (`d` 15 12 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `d` 14 1 2027

-- Arguments: day made, longer period notified, day notified, last day of the longer period, reported, day reported, today.
